{
  "about": "The generated garments the realistic wardrobe is imported from: one entry per source file (matched by the start of its name), with what the intake can't read from the mesh (`kind`, `ease`, `cut_for`, `triangles`) and how closely it follows the body (`conform`: `structured` for jackets and coats, `partial` for sweaters and loose trousers, `moderate` for shirts and jeans, `body` for T-shirts and tank tops, `strong` for leggings) and what the browser needs to know (`also_fills`: a one-piece or a dress takes the bottoms slot too; `frame`: who it is cut for, `masculine`, `feminine` or `unisex`). A top or a jacket is fitted for the bottoms it is worn with: hanging over them (the default), by `worn_most` metres at the most, or, with `\"worn\": \"tucked\"` and layer 0, drawn in under them, for a top that lies on the body (import_generated.py, \"Bottoms first\"). See README.md.",
  "author": "Axcenity",
